{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the matrix of Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen (1993). A directed graph’s edge is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column with one source and one target, which gives the oriented incidence matrix of spectral","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L). The matrix conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Two-bit-planes","level":2,"text":"Two bit planes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sources and the targets are each stored as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a vertex can be on both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sides of a column. Its entry is then target − source = 0, with both bits kept.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"sources(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"targets(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the stars and equality read the planes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so nothing is lost. A directed self-loop is such a column. ","type":"text"},{"code":"reversed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" swaps the planes, negating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every entry, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"transposed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transposes each plane to give the dual. Both are O(1).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Storage is 4·n·m\/8 bytes, so the matrix suits dense or small incidence. ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sparse representation. Equality compares both planes cell for cell, with equal shape, so column","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order counts.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init()","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-1k5cq","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-46tuh","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-6qyfl","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-y850","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(vertexCount:)","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(vertexCount:edges:)","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/init(vertexCount:hyperedges:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/